        "id": 9626,
        "name": "jason_kratz",
        "username": "jason_kratz",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/7c8e57/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-21T22:06:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had an issue come up in a solo game the other day, where The Scholar used Bring What You Need on a deck with 2 cards remaining.</p><p>BWYN causes the top three cards to be revealed, and 2 of those are placed in your hand, one on the bottom of the deck. A reveal cannot trigger a reshuffle, so I only revealed 2 cards. The question is, what do I do with them if I cannot meet the requirements of the power? Obviously, I cannot both put 2 revealed cards in my hand and 1 on the bottom when I have only 2 cards - unless I tear one of the cards in half, which didn't seem to be the right answer.</p><p>I decided that I could choose how to distribute the cards, and of course took both into my hand - did I unintentionally cheat by doing so?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:27.694Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 3,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
